**Commented by Didactylos on 4 Apr 37576242 06:13 UTC**
Replying to [Ageless](comment:2):
Almost correct. Midnight is 00:00 ''and'' 24:00 - although since clocks can't display two values at once, [nearly](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Image:Clock_showing_24_00.JPG) all of them show 00:00. But BOINC treats 24:00 as exactly what it represents; midnight at the end of the day. As you can see, using this value is the only way to specify that BOINC ''never'' compute or connect. Here's the actual code:

```
    if (start==end) return false;
    if (start==0 && end==24) return false;
    if (start==24 && end==0) return true;
    if (start < end) {
        return (hour < start || hour > end);
    } else {
        return (hour >= end && hour < start);
    }
```

